WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.730
A microscope can show you what
a part of a cell looks like.

2
00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:07.480
But to find out what it does,
you need that part on its own,

3
00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:08.960
and plenty of it.

4
00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:11.770
So first, you smash the cells open.

5
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.510
Now every part is mixed
in one soup: nuclei,

6
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:20.240
mitochondria, ribosomes, and
enzymes that could digest the rest.

7
00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:23.670
So how do you get one part out, undamaged?

8
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:28.510
In this mission, you'll find out why taking
cells apart is worth all the trouble.

9
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.330
Then you'll follow the
method, step by step,

10
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.790
keeping the parts you want intact.

11
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.610
Your mission: find out how to get
one part of a cell out, undamaged.
